That vow still stands. To rebuild the kingdom will be a huge task, but I will share her burden.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Although he is yet a child, Atsuo displayed rare fortitude and determination.\par
\par
He certainly has what it takes to grow into a leader. Perhaps one day he will have the chance to govern this village.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell The thought of Prince Faris one day ruling over this realm does not inspire confidence in the kingdom's future...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I hope that Obsidian and I will be able to take part in a race one day. I am confident that I would be a match for anyone\f1\emdash\f0 including you, <pc>.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Princess Jade takes after her father in having a very sweet tooth. I have rarely seen her so content.\par
\par
I shall track down the finest delicacies in this town and present them to her. I consider it nothing less than my duty.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It pains me to admit it, but I do not tend to be lucky in situations such as these.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell King Carnelian would not be happy if he knew I had allowed Princess Jade to return to this terrible place.\par
\par
Might I suggest that we leave as soon as you have finished whatever it is you want to do here.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Princess Jade will not speak to me about what happened in this village. Clearly it affected her deeply.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Such extraordinary creatures. It is no wonder that I feel rather flustered in their presence...\par
\par
...Wait! Please ignore what I said! I did not mean to voice my thoughts!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I shall never forget the moment when Sylvando presented Avarith with that horse dung...\par
\par
The question remains, however... Just how did he carry it around with him? There are some feats I fear I could never equal...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell When we first found Rab up here, I thought he was mummified. I do not scare easily, but I was terrified when he started to move.\par
\par
Even thinking about it makes me shudder. Indeed, I regret mentioning it at all...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I have fond memories of the library back in Heliodor Castle. When I was young, I would compete with my companions to see who could read the most.\par
\par
I loved tales of derring-do and books about magical feats. They were so exciting, it never felt like study.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Three decades have passed, but the memories have not faded. This will always be my home.\par
\par
I pray that my family and friends have returned to Yggdrasil and rest now in peace.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Queen Frysabel must be around the same age as Princess Jade, but she seems much more mature somehow.\par
\par
Perhaps the Princess will become more even-tempered and less impetuous when she takes the throne, but somehow I have my doubts.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It is clear the Watchers have powers that we who dwell on the surface cannot begin to imagine.\par
\par
How else could they have built their homes in the sky, or protected the memories of the first Luminary for so long?\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell The days when I called you Darkspawn are long gone, <pc>. You have let me join you, and for that I am grateful.\par
\par
Now I will do all I can to protect you. I will be your sword, and your shield.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Thank you for allowing me to join you, <pc>... I feel nothing but shame when I think of the times I called you Darkspawn.\par
\par
Know that those days are gone. Now I am at your service, and that of the Princess. I will fight to defend you to the very end.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It sounds as though the Watchers may know something about this dark star.\par
\par
Let us do as our new friend says, and speak with their Elder.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell If our Watcher friend is right, then the Dark One defeated by the first Luminary has returned.\par
\par
It is clear that there is far more to this tale than one could ever hope to guess at. We must not rest until we know the truth.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell The Watchers clearly have knowledge that far surpasses ours. Those floating stones alone are beyond the capabilities of anyone on the surface.\par
\par
Once our battle is at an end, I would very much like to bring craftsmen from Heliodor here. They would learn a great deal, I am sure.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I must confess that I feared the worst when the Elder collapsed.\par
\par
Fortunately, it seems he only needed some sleep. At his age, it is no surprise.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh1162\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell We owe the Elder a great deal. Not only did he grant us new powers, he also presented us with the Wheel of Time.\par
\par
Once we have defeated the Dark One, we should bring him some kind of gift to show our gratitude.\par
\par
Indeed, I know just the thing. The pillowmakers of Heliodor are unparalleled in their craftsmanship. For someone who spends most of their life asleep, a pillow would make an ideal offering.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell More than one Watcher has told me that I remind them of Drustan.\par
\par
I do not see the resemblance myself, but nevertheless it is an honour to be likened to a hero of legend.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell We could never have hoped to reach this place without Cetacea...\par
\par
And the same is true of many other areas, I am sure of it. Let us seek them out.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It appears that the Dark One is protected by some kind of barrier\f1\emdash\f0 one that not even Cetacea can penetrate.\par
\par
All we can do is search out the seedlings and see if they can offer us guidance.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell If we wish to confront the Dark One, we must find a way to penetrate the barrier that surrounds him. I suggest that we speak to someone who has battled with him in the past...\par
\par
Our journey is drawing to a close, <pc>, but first we must find Serenica.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I was born and raised in Zwaardsrust, but I had no idea that the mountains concealed such a secret.\par
\par
They may be mere ruins now, but people made their homes here once...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I was born and raised in Zwaardsrust, but I had no idea that the mountains concealed such a secret.\par
\par
They may be mere ruins now, but people made their homes here once... Perhaps they were the guardians of the sacred seedling?\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I know little about this place, but it is famed for the pilgrims who come here to hone their bodies and minds in the harshest of conditions.\par
\par
Perhaps one day I will return here and test myself. It may well prove educational.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I can understand why you would be drawn to that curious tower, <pc>, but there are other things we must be doing.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell The Dark One will doubtless be a mighty foe, but we should go into battle without fear.\par
\par
My destiny is to protect the Luminary. I will be your sword and your shield, and I will not allow us to be defeated.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Interesting. The floating stones used by the Watchers are also present in this tower.\par
\par
That is fortunate for us. Without them, I fear we would not be able to progress.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell The music that Serena and Veronica played was extraordinary. I, I do not have the words to express how it made me feel.\par
\par
Truly it seemed like a gift from heaven. It is no surprise its power transformed Cetacea.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I wonder if the students here ever have a chance to see their families?\par
\par
It is difficult to live away from home at their age. I admire their fortitude.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell The students here have their whole futures ahead of them.\par
\par
It is our duty to ensure that nothing stands in their way. That is why we must defeat the Dark One, <pc>.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I have never heard of a dark star appearing in the sky, though I confess that there is much of our world's history of which I am ignorant.\par
\par
One thing that I do know for certain, however, is that this does not bode well...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell The forces of Heliodor did this to Cobblestone, and I take full responsibility. I only wish I could have done more to stop it.\par
\par
Still, what is done is done, and now I must attempt to make amends by helping to rebuild the village. I will not rest until it is back on its feet.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell The manner in which Cobblestone has recovered is impressive indeed. The villagers and those who have come to join them have worked hard. They deserve this.\par
\par
The next time we visit, I shall endeavour to bring some delicacies from Heliodor. A celebration is most certainly in order.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I admire anyone who commits to a lifelong union\f1\emdash\f0 especially when they are as youthful as you, <pc>. Perhaps one day I shall do the same.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I do struggle somewhat to imagine you and Erik sharing the same abode.\par
\par
I have never found him to be anything other than companionable, of course, but making the leap to cohabitation is quite a different matter...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh1162\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I have nothing but respect and admiration for Veronica, and I am certain that you shall reside together in harmony for many years to come.\par
\par
Though I must say, her outraged response to Lord Robert's choice of...reading material suggests that you would do well to keep any such...publications of your own well hidden... Ahem...\par
\par
Hmm? You have no such periodicals, you say? Yes, well... I suppose you are the Luminary, after all\f1\emdash\f0 I need not have worried.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Serena may seem meek, but I can confidently say that she possesses the greatest fortitude in our group.\par
\par
Even when surrounded by chaos, she does not allow her wits to abandon her.\par
\par
I suppose that is a different kind strength to that which I possess\f1\emdash\f0 perhaps I could stand to learn a thing or two from her.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It would appear that Sylvando is as comfortable in the domestic realm as he is on the battlefield. I cannot fathom how one man can become so multitalented...\par
\par
I confess, I sometimes fantasise about being as capable around the house as he. What a life that would be...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I trust that you will inform me should the two of you ever be in need of protection?\par
\par
I am more than prepared to assemble a cordon of guards that shall surround your home at all times\f1\emdash\f0 not so much as a mouse shall get through on our watch!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It has long been my desire to study martial arts under Lord Robert's tutelage...\par
\par
As such, I must admit to feeling rather jealous. Now that you are living together, you can have him teach you whenever you wish...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It would be false to claim that I foresaw our current arrangement...\par
\par
But Cobblestone is now my home, and I swear to defend it and its people with my life. Never again shall tragedy strike this village.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It would be false to claim that I foresaw our current arrangement...\par
\par
But life is full of surprises\f1\emdash\f0 I would not have expected to take much pleasure in going on walks, either, and now I can think of little I enjoy more. If time permits, I should like to pay Cobblestone Tor a visit...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It seems that everyone in Cobblestone climbs the Tor when they come of age...\par
\par
The Heliodorian army also has its own rites of passage. I remember having to take on my first dracky. A most frightening experience.\par
\par
I am sure there are similar rituals wherever you go in the world. It is important to mark the moment when one leaves their childhood behind.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh1162\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Nothing is more heartening than the presence of an ally who can be trusted in battle. I am truly glad to have you by my side, <pc>.\par
\par
However, I must apologise for demanding that you draw your sword... Alas, I have never been the best with people...\par
\par
Still, I was able to sense your strength and determination anew as our blades clashed. I swear to continue to serve as your sword and shield until the day I am no longer needed.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Truly, you are a man of formidable strength\f1\emdash\f0 you have come on in leaps and bounds since the day you were cast into the castle dungeon.\par
\par
Now, let us proceed to the top of the Tor. Please do not ask why.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell As a soldier of Heliodor, it is my sworn duty to protect the people of this realm.\par
\par
Now, however, I have others to protect\f1\emdash\f0 I must fight for the peace and security of all the people of the world.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell As a humble servant of Heliodor, I know how much the return of Princess Jade means to the people of this kingdom.\par
\par
In a world filled with so much darkness and despair, she will bring the light of hope into their lives.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell He may be gone, but my old friend's spirit lives on within me.\par
\par
Do not misunderstand me, I am not asking you to forgive him. We should not forget what he did\f1\emdash\f0 but nor should we forget what he once was.\par
\par
With his strength and my own combined, we will fight for you until the end. Together we will be your sword, your shield, your unswerving companions.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell This is not your fight. I must face Jasper alone. This is a darkness I helped create and I alone must end it.\par
\par
Please, <pc>. We must return to the balcony. A battle awaits me there that I cannot and will not avoid.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell That dark figure seems to know about my past, and that of Jasper. I wonder, could it really be...?\par
\par
Come, <pc>. Let us go after it. I feel that it has something important it wants to show us...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I get the distinct feeling that black shadow has something it wishes to tell me.\par
\par
If we track it down, I believe we will learn more. Come, let us follow it without delay.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell My duty is to protect the people of Heliodor, no matter how rich or poor they may be.\par
\par
Whatever the future holds, I shall not waver in my resolve. I would gladly lay down my life to defend this kingdom.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell The swords of Hotto are not like those we use in Heliodor. The blades are curved, with just one sharpened edge...\par
\par
Indeed, there is one legendary blade forged in this village that I have always wanted to wield. Perhaps we will come across it one day...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I lost my whole family when Zwaardsrust was attacked by monsters, but somehow I survived and was taken in by the King of Heliodor.\par
\par
We were not related, but still he treated me like his own flesh and blood. I think of him as a father.\par
\par
Without him, I do not think I would have made it. I will never forget what he did for me. I owe him my life.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell The star's true nature remains shrouded in mystery...\par
\par
Let us do as the Seer said and call on Cetacea. We must pay a visit to the Watchers.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Does the Dark One truly conceal himself within that star? All I know is that he pollutes this world with his evil.\par
\par
...Can you hear me, Calasmos? We will defeat you! Of that, there is no doubt!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Gallopolis prides itself on the fighting prowess of its desert knights, but even they will struggle to defend the people from the monsters threatening the kingdom.\par
\par
Still, we have no choice but to leave this fight to them. We must focus on dealing with that dark star.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell We have dealt with the immediate threat, but while that dark star hangs in the sky, the monsters will continue to rampage.\par
\par
The evil must be cut off at source, before it is too late.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It seems the dark star is doing its baneful work\f1\emdash\f0 it has driven the monsters to overrun the town.\par
\par
We will not leave it at their mercy, however. We shall not rest until every last one of these beasts has been slain!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I dislike talking about it, but the statue they built of me here was to commemorate my part in the battle for Dundrasil all those years ago.\par
\par
It does not become a warrior to boast of his achievements. I was simply doing my duty. I have no need of plaudits or praise, and certainly not of statues.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell This is where Arachtagon sought refuge after we did battle...\par
\par
I remember landing a blow to his left eye, but somehow he survived. I dearly wish I had finished him when I had the chance.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell This is my home, <pc>. I was but a small boy when the monsters came, but I remember it as though it were yesterday.\par
\par
I lost everything that day, but I vowed that I would become strong and do all that was in my power to prevent anyone else suffering as I had.\par
\par
Nothing has changed. I still live by that vow. We must restore peace to Erdrea. Its people have suffered enough.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Your father was a respected king, sure enough, but he was also far more than that. He was a peerless warrior and fine leader of men on the battlefield.\par
\par
I always respected him deeply, and to this day I aim to emulate him in all I do.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I know it is too late for apologies now, but when I think back to the time I tried to capture you and Princess Jade here, I feel deeply ashamed.\par
\par
Well, at least some good came of it. This was where I began to doubt whether you were truly the Darkspawn. I just wish I had realised the truth sooner.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Though I was here on that fateful night, I could not save your father's life...\par
\par
Nor could I save King Carnelian from what Mordegon did to him. Even thinking about it pains me still.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell The powerful weapon of which Don Rodrigo spoke proved to be working together. As long as we trust each other, we will be more than the sum of our parts.\par
\par
That is the only way to erase the dark star from the sky. Once again, Don Rodrigo has proven that his wisdom is beyond compare.\par
\par
If we can make use of the powers he has taught us, nothing can stand in our way.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I have heard tales of the legendary trials undergone by the knights of Puerto Valor. Now it seems it is my turn to join them.\par
\par
I will not do this alone, however. Sylvando and I shall join forces and do battle with whatever foes await us in the Kingsbarrow.\par
\par
Let us take this trial and claim the mighty weapon of which Don Rodrigo spoke\f1\emdash\f0 and let us hope that it shall give us the power to rid the world of the dark star.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I trained here under Don Rodrigo in my youth, and Norberto\f1\emdash\f0 forgive me, Sylvando\f1\emdash\f0 was my fellow student.\par
\par
He has changed a great deal since I last saw him, of course. It is little wonder it took me such a long time to work it out.\par
\par
There was always something strangely familiar about him, however. I felt as though I had always known him, somehow.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell This town has changed greatly since I came here as a young man. Building a casino here would have been unthinkable back then...\par
\par
I have no interest in such places\f1\emdash\f0 do what you have to do and then let us leave.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I learned from one of the villagers here that you once defeated a tentacular that was terrorising the ocean to the west.\par
\par
I have fought a few of the beasts in my time, but I always had a whole troop of men with me. I am impressed by your derring-do, <pc>.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I did once hear of a place to the west where ships would vanish without trace...and now it seems we are here.\par
\par
There is indeed something unusual about this area. It is easy to imagine that people would just disappear and never be heard from again...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I understand that this grey gordon creature was imprisoning people and forcing them to dance for him...\par
\par
Alas, I still fail to see what the purpose of it all might have been. Could anyone enlighten me?\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Are you familiar with this kind of dance, <pc>? I am afraid it leaves me somewhat cold.\par
\par
Music was never something in which I had much interest, to be honest, though I still remember the marching songs of my youth fondly.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Surely not... Surely we have not actually entered the picture...?\par
\par
I have found myself in some unexpected places since joining you, <pc>, but none as odd as this.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell When this kingdom was frozen, I was dispatched from Heliodor at the request of Queen Frysabel.\par
\par
I entrusted the hunt for the Luminary to my deputies and rode out here to see what was happening...\par
\par
But of course, I could do little for the kingdom in the end. It was you who saved it, <pc>, and yet I did not know you were a force for good at the time...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Queen Frysabel and Krystalinda have joined forces, proving once more that old foes can put the past behind them.\par
\par
Krystalinda may have frozen the kingdom, but in the end, she did no serious harm. It is most noble of the Queen to allow her to make amends for her actions.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell The beast we vanquished had defended the kingdom against the witch for centuries...\par
\par
We made a most terrible mistake. We were outsmarted by the witch and did her dirty work for her. The shame shall forever be seared into my soul.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It seems that countless ancient tomes are stored in the library's vaults.\par
\par
Perhaps they could shed light on some of the mysteries of our world. I will recommend that the King dispatches Heliodor's finest scholars to investigate further.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Truly, the powers of the Luminary never cease to amaze me. By wielding the Sword of Light, you saved that child from a truly terrible fate.\par
\par
Your destiny is to give the world hope, and mine is to be your sword and your shield, and to do all that I can to protect you.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Something is troubling Erik, there can be no doubt about that.\par
\par
If there is anything we can do to help him, we should. We owe it to him.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Arboria has a deep connection to Erdwin and the heroes of legend\f1\emdash\f0 the ones who first did battle with the Dark One.\par
\par
Let us speak to the people here and see if they can aid us in our quest to rid the world of the dark star.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell To think, if Dundrasil had not fallen, you would have undergone training here as part of your education as Crown Prince.\par
\par
Things panned out differently in the end, but it seems that fate has brought you here nonetheless. Let us undergo the training\f1\emdash\f0 I sense it will have much to teach us.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It is most curious. It is my first time here, and yet it feels strangely familiar...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Rab mentioned that students come here to hone their bodies and minds to the limit...\par
\par
I have no idea what the training entails, but I must confess that I am rather interested in experiencing it for myself.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Such extraordinary creatures. It is no wonder that I feel rather flustered in their presence...\par
\par
...Wait! Please ignore what I said! I did not mean to voice my thoughts!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I was always more suited to doing battle on land. It was Jasper who excelled at naval warfare.\par
\par
In fact, he commanded the fleet that defended the coast of Heliodor, and he did it with utter dedication. ...Why, Jasper...? Why did you allow yourself to be tempted by the darkness?\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It is extraordinary to think that we were capable of forging a new Sword of Light!\par
\par
Truly, it feels as if we are following in the footsteps of Erdwin and the heroes of legend.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell How extraordinary...\par
\par
I have no idea how this place was constructed\f1\emdash\f0 and I suspect that questions of who built it and how shall forever remain a mystery.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Miko spoke of a forge called the Crucible, hidden in the heart of the volcano. Could that possibly be true?\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It is hard to believe that there is anyone still living here, on this ancient battlefield...\par
\par
Such a person must be some form of angel...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Urgh! This heat is something else! It feels like my axe could melt. And that would be a terrible...axe-ident.\par
\par
...I'm sorry. I wish I had never said that. This relentless heat appears to have relieved me of my senses.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell I have known the name Drustan since I was a boy.\par
\par
To think that he constructed this place and that it still stands is truly extraordinary.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It seems these magic circles can transport us from one part of the labyrinth to another.\par
\par
Let us see where each of them takes us. It will save on boot leather, and we may find ourselves somewhere rather unexpected.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh871\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell It seems it is no coincidence that I fight alongside the Luminary. That is what Drustan implied.\par
\par
It is curious. I feel a bond with him. Meeting him was not like meeting a stranger.\par
\par
We both have roots in Zwaardsrust, of course, but perhaps there is more to the bond that ties us together...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell The people of Zwaardsrust have always held Drustan in the highest esteem. After all, he is our kingdom's founder.\par
\par
To be able to trace our roots to one of the legendary heroes who defeated the Dark One is the greatest of honours.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Can you feel it, <pc>? We are growing ever stronger.\par
\par
We are honing our fighting skills, just as Drustan intended.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell This place is vast, and yet you seem to know where you are going.\par
\par
Surely you cannot have been here before...? In any case, lead the way. I shall follow.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell Not only is Drustan one of the first Luminary's companions, he is also the founder of my home, Zwaardsrust.\par
\par
To think, he has awaited us since the Age of Heroes. Truly, it is an honour to meet him.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell ...Hm?\par
\par
We must be careful. I sense someone's presence...\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell We cannot stand aside and watch while Erdrea is in danger. Let us head for the Tower, <pc>.\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx973\cellx10352 
\pard\intbl Hendrik\cell ...... \cell\row 
